"lines": [
"A dead man's pockets held two notes the FBI still can't read.",
"Over thirty lines of letters, numbers, and brackets.",
"Ricky McCormick, forty-one, was found in a Missouri cornfield. Cause of death: undetermined.",
"FBI codebreakers crack almost every cipher. This one stopped them at step two.",
"They couldn't even tell what kind of code it was.",
"The American Cryptogram Association tried too. No breakthrough.",
"So in twenty eleven, the bureau asked the public for help.",
"Tips poured in. The bureau had to build a page just for theories.",
"The FBI said his family told them he'd used codes since boyhood.",
"But his family says Ricky could barely write his name.",
"One cipher expert thinks he never wrote them. Maybe he was a courier.",
"So who wrote the code he carried?",
"Decades later, the case is still open.",
"Nobody explained it."
